@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# scriptc 0.4.7 vs @chttp 0.4.x
+
+Evidence from compiling this tree with `scriptc` **0.4.7** (CLI from a sibling
+install). Workspace `package.json` still listed `0.3.6` when the probe started.
+
+T3's Phase 2 wanted `@chttp/val` as contracts-lite because Effect-Schema
+generics fail (SC8010/SC2001). That is an **Effect** problem, not a `@chttp/val`
+problem: val is already inside the subset.
+
+## What compiles (100% static)
+
+After `pnpm -r build` (router `dist/` must exist for gates that import the
+package name `@chttp/router`):
+
+| Entry | 0.4.7 `scriptc coverage` | `scriptc build` ELF |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `packages/val/src/index.ts` | 680/680 (100%) | n/a (library) |
+| `bench/apps/chttp-val.ts` | 2366 (100%) | yes |
+| `bench/apps/chttp-fetch.ts` (router) | 1770 (100%) | (same graph as existing fetch gates) |
+| `bench/apps/chttp-stream.ts` | 1901 (100%) | yes |
+| `packages/static/gate.ts` | 2065 (100%) | yes |
+| `packages/mcp/gate.ts` | 1335 (100%) | yes |
+| `bench/apps/chttp-html.ts` | 1795 (100%) | (gate only) |
+| `packages/auth/gate.ts` | 506 (100%) | (gate only) |
+| `packages/stream/src/index.ts --npm-static @chttp/router` | 207 (100%) | n/a |
+
+**T3 fork command (program-code, preferred):**
+
+```sh
+pnpm add @chttp/router @chttp/val @chttp/mcp @chttp/static @chttp/stream
+scriptc build app.ts
+# or, when compiling published dist JS:
+scriptc build app.ts --npm-static @chttp/router,@chttp/val,@chttp/mcp,@chttp/static,@chttp/stream
+```
+
+`@chttp/val` does not need `--npm-static` when the app imports its `src` the
+way `bench/apps/chttp-val.ts` does.
+
+## Before / after: `packages/stream/src/index.ts` without `--npm-static`
+
+**Before** (router still named `ReadableStreamReadResult`):
+
+```
+not analyzable: 1 TypeScript error
+
+packages/router/src/index.ts:1860:30 - error SC0001: Cannot find name 'ReadableStreamReadResult'.
+  function (v: ReadableStreamReadResult<Uint8Array>): void {
+               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+Expected: typecheck like the fetch gates (same file, relative import).
+Actual: when the file is reached through `@chttp/router/src/index.ts` from
+stream, scriptc has no DOM name `ReadableStreamReadResult`.
+
+**After** (this PR): the callback takes `unknown` and narrows with `as`.
+`scriptc coverage packages/stream/src/index.ts` typechecks (93% static: `Ctx`
+without a concrete instance is unreached, as `packages/stream/AGENTS.md` already
+documents). The bench gate stays 100%.
+
+This is a **scriptc lib/DOM-gap**, worked around in-tree. Sibling issue title:
+
+> SC0001: `ReadableStreamReadResult` is unresolved when a file is pulled via package `./src` export
+
+Repro: `scriptc coverage packages/stream/src/index.ts` on chttp main before the
+annotation change. Expected: analyze. Actual: SC0001 on that identifier.
+
+## Remaining: `@chttp/unplugin` (package, not a T3 ELF path)
+
+`scriptc coverage packages/unplugin/src/index.ts` → **97%** static.
+
+Blockers (SC2013), not Effect generics:
+
+- `typescript` — import resolves to `typescript.d.ts`, not runtime JS; TS
+  compiler API / `forEachChild` / AST node field reads (SC1090) in unreached
+  code.
+- `unplugin` — `createRequire` result escapes (static requires need literals).
+- `picomatch` — several SC1090/SC2020 fences (`string.split` on `RegExp | string`,
+  `string & any[].map`).
+
+unplugin is a **Vite/webpack build-time** plugin. It must not be linked into a
+T3 native ELF. No in-tree rewrite will make `typescript` + `unplugin` compile
+natively; that would be a scriptc island or "don't compile this package".
+
+Suggested scriptc issue (only if they want plugin authors to compile):
+
+> SC2013: `typescript` package import resolves to `.d.ts`, not JS
+
+Repro: `import ts from "typescript"` in any program, `scriptc coverage`.
+Expected: either refuse with a clear "use a Node island" or resolve
+`typescript/lib/typescript.js`. Actual: SC2013 pointing at the `.d.ts`.
+
+## False alarm (needs `pnpm -r build`)
+
+`packages/static/gate.ts` importing `@chttp/router` reports SC0001 "Cannot find
+module" **until** `packages/router/dist` exists. CI already builds first.
+This is not a 0.4.7 regression (0.3.6 behaves the same).
+
+## Not observed here
+
+SC8010 / SC2001 Effect-Schema generics do **not** appear in `@chttp/val` or
+the chttp gates. They appear when a program imports `effect`. Use val for
+Tier 2; do not wait on scriptc generic-erasure to adopt chttp.
