 - Use `s.charAt(i)`, never `s[i]` (SC1090). Named imports from `node:http` only. Guard `T | undefined` explicitly (`x !== null && x !== undefined`).
 - `scriptc < 0.3.2` had no backpressure: `write()` result, `"drain"`, `writableLength` and write callbacks were all refused. On 0.3.2+ a compiled `Writable` subclass (runtime-owned surface; never override `push`) wraps `res` and observes the real queue. `ServerResponse` itself still refuses `drain`/`writableLength`/a boolean `write()`, so the wrapper — not `res` — is the backpressure surface. The pending-bytes window cap stays as the secondary fail-safe.
 - A subclassed `_write` does not pump when the class ships inside a statically compiled npm package: `write()` buffers forever and returns false. `ResWriter` probes the pump at construction (swallowed sentinel chunk) and falls back to direct sink writes; see `bench/scriptc-evidence/ws-backpressure-package-mode-2026-10-15.txt`. In that fallback the probe keeps `writableLength` at 1 forever — don't read it as a backpressure signal there.
-- A `Ctx` parameter only lowers when a call site gives it a concrete instance, so `scriptc coverage` on `src/index.ts` alone reports unreached code. The gate is `scriptc coverage bench/apps/chttp-stream.ts`, which must stay 100% static.
+- A `Ctx` parameter only lowers when a call site gives it a concrete instance, so `scriptc coverage` on `src/index.ts` alone reports unreached code. The gate is `scriptc coverage bench/apps/chttp-stream.ts`, which must stay 100% static. Compiling `src/index.ts` as the entry needs `--npm-static @chttp/router` or the in-tree relative graph; a missing DOM name on the router side is SC0001 (see `bench/scriptc-evidence/scriptc-0.4.7-chttp-packages.md`).
 - `pnpm --filter @chttp/stream test` runs the node:test suite against the tsc build with real HTTP round-trips. The compiled path is smoked by building `examples/sse-clock` and `curl -N` (events at the interval; the interval must stop after disconnect).
